# Agentic Coding

## Long-Horizon Work
- Focus on incremental progress by layer (model -> service -> controller -> screen).
- Complete one layer systematically before moving to the next.
- Never generate an entire feature (BE + Mobile) in one response unless explicitly asked.

## State Tracking
- Keep track of progress clearly for large tasks.
- Reference the SRS use cases (UC01–UC33) and Business Rules (BR-01–BR-30) when implementing features.
- Before starting a new feature, confirm which Use Case it corresponds to.

## Safety and Autonomy
- Take local, reversible actions freely: reading files, editing code.
- Ask before actions that are destructive or hard to reverse (e.g., dropping DB collections, changing auth logic).
- Do NOT touch payment/wallet code (SePay/HMAC) without explicit confirmation — transactions are immutable by design.

## Research and Exploration
- For complex investigations, search both `backend/src/` and `mobile/src/` systematically.
- Check `store/authStore.js` before writing any auth-related mobile code.
- Check `src/services/api.js` before adding new API calls.

## File Creation Discipline
- Backend new feature: create in `backend/src/features/<name>/` (4 files: routes, controller, service, model).
- Mobile new feature: create in `mobile/src/features/<name>/` (api.js + hooks/ + components/).
- If temporary/test files are created, clean them up before declaring done.

## Subagent Judgment
- Use parallel work only when backend and mobile tasks are truly independent.
- For tightly-coupled features (e.g., API + screen using that API), work sequentially.